/ The email editor (TessEdit). The editor keeps the hidden fields up to date;
/ Nuntius::EmailDesignParams takes them in the controller.
/ Locals: record, name (the form's param key), document, lock (optional),
/ media_url (optional: the images Image blocks choose from, MediaController)
/ With images, they are named in the document, with URLs for the canvas,
/ and the preview compiles with them shown (MediaController#compile).
/ variables (optional: the record's variable_roots) has the editor suggest
/ them, when the host app mounts Liquidum (Nuntius::Variables.url).
/ translations_url (optional: Admin::TranslationsController's) shows and
/ edits its t filters' translations.
/ options (optional): the editor's options, e.g. {template: true} for a
/ template's own root fields (app/javascript/nuntius/blocks/email.js).
/ attributes (optional): the record's attributes edited in the editor, whose
/ errors show above it. slots (optional): the form's own fields for the
/ editor's slot fields, as data-tess-edit-target="slot" elements.
/ frame (optional, default true): false when it fills an unpadded tab.
- lock = local_assigns[:lock]
- frame = local_assigns.fetch(:frame, true)
- media_url = local_assigns[:media_url]
/ (an empty one when its class has none, so the variables controller can point it at another)
- variables_url = (Nuntius::Variables.url(self, local_assigns[:variables]) || "") if local_assigns.key?(:variables)
- document = Nuntius::EmailImages.new(record).normalize(document, **image_url_options) if media_url && document
- compile_url = media_url ? "#{media_url}/compile" : tess_edit.compile_path
- problems = record.errors[:base] + [:mjml, *local_assigns[:attributes]].flat_map { |attribute| record.errors.full_messages_for(attribute) }
- if problems.any?
  .rounded-md.border.border-red-200.bg-red-50.px-3.py-2.text-sm.text-red-700 class=(frame ? "mb-3" : "m-4") role="alert"
    - problems.each do |problem|
      p = problem
div class="h-[80vh]" data-controller="tess-edit" data-tess-edit-sample-value="false" data-tess-edit-frame-value=frame.to_s data-tess-edit-compile-url-value=compile_url data-tess-edit-lock-value=(lock&.to_json) data-tess-edit-media-url-value=media_url data-tess-edit-variables-url-value=variables_url data-tess-edit-translations-url-value=local_assigns[:translations_url] data-tess-edit-options-value=local_assigns[:options]&.to_json
  = hidden_field_tag "#{name}[design_json]", document.to_json, id: nil, data: {tess_edit_target: "jsonInput"}
  = hidden_field_tag "#{name}[design_mjml]", "", id: nil, data: {tess_edit_target: "mjmlInput"}
  = local_assigns[:slots]
